# Windows MEMD Client

User-mode client for the MEMD kernel driver on Windows.

## Building

```sh
# With MinGW:
gcc -Wall -O2 -I. -o memd_client.exe memd_client.c

# With MSVC:
cl /W4 /O2 memd_client.c
```

## Usage

```sh
memd_client.exe [process_name]
```

## Files

- `client.h` — Windows DeviceIoControl wrapper (MEMD_DEVICE_NAME)
- `memd_client.c` — Example client program
- `driver.h` — WDM kernel driver header (IOCTL codes, structs, device extension)
- `driver.c` — WDM kernel driver implementation (requires WDK to compile)
- `Makefile` — Build script (MinGW for client, WDK for driver)

## Driver

The kernel driver (`driver.c` / `driver.h`) implements:
- Device creation and symbolic link
- IOCTL dispatch (read/write memory, find process, hide, give root, etc.)
- Process enumeration via PsGetProcessImageFileName
- Memory read/write via KeStackAttachProcess
- Address translation via MmGetPhysicalAddress

Compile with WDK: msbuild or make from WDK command prompt.

## Notes

- Requires the MEMD kernel driver to be installed and running.
- IOCTL codes use CTL_CODE with base 0x8000.
- The driver requires Windows 10/11 x64.

